@startuml
title E09 - Signed firmware update and recovery
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Development / test engineer" as Engineer
control "B06\nFleet/config" as B06
control "S03\nFirmware security/update" as S03
control "H07\nHub lifecycle/config" as H07
control "N04\nNode lifecycle" as N04
control "Hub bootloader / OTA slot" as HubBoot
control "Node bootloader / OTA slot" as NodeBoot
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
control "T02\nHardware-in-loop tools" as T02
Engineer -> B06: Publish board-bound version/hash/signature manifest
B06 -> S03: Check board identity, version monotonicity, hash text and signature verifier
S03 --> B06: Return accept/reject with reason
B06 -> H07: Stage accepted hub update policy/config
H07 -> HubBoot: Download to inactive slot and verify real image signature
B06 -> N04: Open authorized node service/update window
N04 -> NodeBoot: Stage and verify node image
HubBoot -> B08: Report boot health, rollback or confirmed version
NodeBoot -> B08: Report node update result
T02 -> HubBoot: Inject corrupt/wrong-board/reset recovery cases
T02 -> NodeBoot: Verify prior image remains recoverable
note over S03,T02: Current implementation is only the fail-closed policy seam; production crypto and secure boot are pending.
note over Engineer,T02: Outcome - Only authenticated board-compatible upgrades can activate, and failure returns to a known-good image with auditable evidence.
@enduml
